==============================================================================
1. Quranic Arabic Corpus
==============================================================================
License: GNU General Public License (GPL)
Source:  https://corpus.quran.com
Attribution: Quranic Arabic Corpus (University of Leeds), morphology v0.4, via the
             corrected fork https://github.com/mustafa0x/quran-morphology
Details: Lemmas, roots, parts of speech, verb forms, clitic segmentation and frequencies
         for every word - the basis of the curriculum.

==============================================================================
2. Verse translations (alquran.cloud editions)
==============================================================================
Source:  https://alquran.cloud
Details: Saheeh International (en), Muhiuddin Khan (bn), Fateh Muhammad Jalandhry (ur),
         Suhel Farooq Khan & Saifur Rahman Nadwi (hi), Indonesian Ministry of Religious
         Affairs (id), Diyanet Isleri (tr), Mohammad Mahdi Fooladvand (fa),
         Muhammad Hamidullah (fr).

==============================================================================
3. Greentech Apps Foundation (GTAF)
==============================================================================
Source:  https://quran.gtaf.org
Details: Word-by-word glosses (the source of every word meaning) in English, Bangla,
         Urdu, Hindi, Indonesian, Turkish, Farsi and French.

